<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
   Axiom Calc : user-facing strings
  ============================================================================
   Every string here is referenced. `./gradlew lintDebug` reports
   UnusedResources for anything that is not, and CI publishes that report, so a
   dead entry cannot accumulate silently. 67 entries that nothing referenced
   were removed after the first real lint run; the rule they are held to is:

   * Text produced INSIDE a @Composable comes from here, through
     stringResource(). That includes TalkBack labels, which is why the
     accessibility section below exists and is wired into DisplayPanel, the
     keypad, the memory indicator, the angle-mode chip and the favourites
     toggle rather than being hardcoded at those call sites.

   * Text produced by a ViewModel or by the domain layer stays in code. Those
     classes are ordinary JVM classes so the unit suite can assert on them
     without Robolectric or an Android Context: CalcKey carries the TalkBack
     description of every key, RetentionPolicy carries its own retention label,
     and HistoryViewModel produces the "Today"/"Yesterday" group headings. A
     parallel resource for the same words would be a second vocabulary that
     nothing reads, so none is declared.

   The application ships English only and says so in res/xml/locales_config.xml.
   No hardcoded claim is made about Bangladesh VAT or tax law: rates in the
   Formula Calculator are entered by the user and labelled as user-provided.
  ============================================================================
-->
